    "version": 14,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed. — source of truth. Req ID prefix: **HPC**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Req ID** | **Functional Area** | **Sub-Functional Area** | **Requirement** | **Status** | **Comments** | **User Stories** |\n| HPC-001 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should serve all homepage content from Contentful as the sole CMS across all regional storefronts. | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Product Names/Prices - SFCC vs Contentful - Review with @Tim Lavelle  @Jasmijn Tsang | [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=(text%20~%20%22HPC-001\\*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22HPC-001\\*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20HPC-001)%20and%20project%20in%20(SFCC)%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=(text%20~%20%22HPC-001*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22HPC-001*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20HPC-001)%20and%20project%20in%20(SFCC)%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC) |\n| HPC-002 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should provide a Contentful preview environment for authors to validate content before publishing to production. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-002> |\n| HPC-003 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should manage all images and video assets through the CMS media library. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-003> |\n| HPC-004 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support videos referenced via embed URL within CMS content entries. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-004> |\n| HPC-005 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support locale-specific homepage content across all regional storefronts. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-005> |\n| HPC-006 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should ingest translated content from Transperfect into the correct CMS locale fields upon delivery, triggered once content is marked as ready for translation. | Confirmed | EK - We need to discuss the translation strategy/ workflow.  Preference is for translation memory and workflow to live in the CMS, with an integration to Transperfect for human review. Review with @Tim Lavelle | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-006> |\n| HPC-007 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should allow regional authors to publish locale-specific content without affecting other storefronts. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-007> |\n| /HPC-008 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support a full-width hero banner with CMS-managed imagery, copy and CTA links. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-008> |\n| HPC-009 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support editorial modules including campaign imagery, collection features and product spotlights. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-009> |\n| HPC-010 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support reusable page builder templates across page types. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-010> |\n| HPC-011 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support a global and local content model where some content is global (e.g. Sustainability, Fashion Show Hub pages) and some is localised (e.g. policy pages). | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-011> |\n| HPC-012 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support live stream embedding on editorial pages via a structured CMS solution, replacing the current approach of raw HTML code snippets. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-012> |\n| HPC-013 | Homepage & Content | Consent & Cookie Management | The system should grey out all site content and prevent interaction with all site elements when the Didomi consent notice is displayed. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-013> |\n| HPC-014 | Homepage & Content | Consent & Cookie Management | The system should remove the grey out effect and restore full site interactivity once the customer has completed the Didomi consent flow. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-014> |\n| HPC-015 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a sticky global header visible at the top of the screen on all pages and devices. | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Header sticky / non-sticky - pending motion design as well @Jasmijn Tsang | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-015> |\n| HPC-016 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display the Zimmermann brand logo linking back to the homepage. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D